fields.doc:
Quote-ccy unit for the BUY-side cost-breakdown sentence (mirror of the
limit sibling's `total_unit`). Kotlin uses this as the funding-ccy on BUY;
on SELL it reads the base ccy off the amount-row `TradingNumber.symbol`.

F-5 — warm xStock multiplier for the tradfi Amount-explanation sheet;
None (non-stock / BE-absent) -> the mapper renders "--". Replaces the
cold (bizInfo as? SpotInstrument)?.xStockMultiplier.

variants.doc:
Block + show toast + focus a field. V1 contract: BUY uses
`pr_trade_placeorder_inputfield_min_total` with `{num, ccy}` args;
SELL uses `pr_trade_placeorder_inputfield_min_amount` likewise.

